{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Vanessa Works the Evening Shift"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Making a Change"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 6}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Exchange advice and suggestions in communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Conditional Sentences"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">zero conditional</span> when the result of the condition is always true, like a scientific fact.<br/><br/>In other conditional sentences, like the First and Second Conditional, you are thinking about a particular condition in the future, and the result of this condition. There is <span class=\"strong\">not</span> a real possibility that this condition will happen. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">The Zero Conditional</span><br/>Notice that you are thinking about a result that is always true for this condition. You are not thinking about the future or the past, or even the present.<br/><span class=\"italic\">Example: If I go to bed earlier, I feel more rested the next day.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Simple</span> tense to write the zero conditional. The important thing about the zero conditional is that the condition is a general truth.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Other Conditional Sentences</span><br/>In the first conditional, we use Simple Present and Simple Future to talk about a particular situation in the future. <br> Example: <span class=\"italic\">If it rains, the streets will get wet.</span>  <br><br> In the second conditional, we use Past Simple and would + base verb to talk about an unreal or imaginary situations in the present or the future.  <br> Example: <span class=\"italic\">If I won the lottery, I would buy a new house.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Note that you do not need a comma when you write the condition before the result."}, {"type": "example", "content": " If it rains, the streets will get wet."}, {"type": "example", "content": "When it rains, the streets get wet."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you ride your bike, you get there faster."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If I won the lottery, I would buy a new house."}, {"type": "example", "content": " I would buy a new house if I won the lottery."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If I had a chauffeur, I wouldn't have to walk."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "exhausted"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to be very tired that you have no energy left"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Sally is so exhausted from her demanding job."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le06ob05aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about healthy or unhealthy situations at work."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "beat"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an informal way to say you're tired"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Peter is beat because he just came back from the gym."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le06ob05aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "relief"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "when something unpleasant or painful has gone away"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If Sally went to the gym, she would get some relief from her stress."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le06ob05aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to overwork "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "working overtime on a regular basis"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If Peter became the boss, he would not overwork his employees."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le06ob05aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "optimal"}, {"type": "definition", 